<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 1 July, from 1097 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1097 CE <span class="tih-ago">929 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders defeat the Seljuk Turks at Dorylaeum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a> routed the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-i">Kilij Arslan I</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorylaeum">Dorylaeum</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. The victory opened the road across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> and showed that the crusaders could beat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> in open battle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1690 CE <span class="tih-ago">336 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William III defeats James II at the Battle of the Boyne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William of Orange defeated the deposed James II on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-boyne">River Boyne</a> in Ireland (1 July Old Style). The victory secured the Protestant succession and is still commemorated by the Orange Order each July.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/continental-congress.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1776 CE <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Continental Congress debates independence in a decisive test vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting as a committee of the whole, Congress debated Richard Henry Lee's resolution for independence; nine colonies backed it in a test vote. The formal vote followed the next day with twelve in favour.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1862 CE <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union guns repel Lee's assaults at Malvern Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Massed Union artillery shattered Confederate attacks at Malvern Hill near Richmond, the last of the Seven Days Battles. Though McClellan withdrew afterwards, Lee's costly assaults ended the campaign.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1863 CE <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Gettysburg begins in Pennsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate and Union forces collided at Gettysburg, opening the largest battle ever fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Three days later Lee's army withdrew, having suffered some 23,000 of the roughly 50,000 casualties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1916 CE <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British army suffers 57,470 casualties on the first day of the Somme</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a week-long bombardment, British and French infantry attacked along the Somme. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> lost 57,470 men killed, wounded or missing, the heaviest single-day toll in the British Army's history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1997 CE <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain hands Hong Kong back to China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At midnight <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> passed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, ending 156 years of British rule. The territory became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/special-administrative-regions-of-china">Special Administrative Region</a> under the 'one country, two systems' principle.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a></div></div></li></ol>
